Module 2 — Linux Commands Cheat Sheet

Getting Information
-------------------
Return your username: whoami
Return your user & group ID: id
Return OS name & system info: uname -a
Manual for a command: man <command>
Search man pages: man -k .
Help for a command: <command> --help
Current date/time: date

Navigating Directories
----------------------
List files by date: ls -lrt
Find all .sh files: find -name "*.sh"
Print working directory: pwd
Make directory: mkdir <dir>
Go up one level: cd ../
Go home: cd ~
Change directory: cd <path>
Remove directory: rmdir <dir> -v

Monitoring System
-----------------
List processes: ps
List all processes: ps -e
System usage: top
Disk usage: df

File Operations
---------------
Create empty file: touch <file>
Copy file: cp <src> <dest>
Move/rename file: mv <src> <dest>
Delete file: rm <file> -v

Permissions
-----------
Add execute for all: chmod +x <file>
Add execute for user: chmod u+x <file>
Remove read for group & others: chmod go-r <file>

Viewing Contents
----------------
Show file: cat <file>
Page view: more <file>
First 10 lines: head -10 <file>
Last 10 lines: tail -10 <file>
Print text/variable: echo "text", echo $VAR

Text Wrangling
--------------
Sort: sort <file>
Sort reverse: sort -r <file>
Remove duplicates: uniq <file>

Counts
------
Lines: wc -l <file>
Words: wc -w <file>
Chars: wc -m <file>

Grep
----
Case-insensitive whole-word match:
grep -iw <pattern> <file>

Find files containing pattern:
grep -l <pattern> *.txt

Cut & Paste
-----------
Merge files: paste f1 f2 f3
Merge with comma: paste -d "," f1 f2 f3
Extract first column: cut -d "," -f 1 <file>
Extract bytes 2–5: cut -b 2-5 <file>
Extract from byte 10: cut -b 10- <file>

Compression
-----------
Create archive: tar -cvf file.tar.gz f1 f2
Zip files: zip file.zip f1 f2
Unzip: unzip file.zip
Unzip to directory: unzip file.zip -d <dir>

Networking
----------
Hostname: hostname
Ping: ping <url>
Interfaces: ip
Show URL contents: curl <url>
Download file: wget <url>
